## Request

Extend the existing dashboard vertical slice without creating a second authority. Read the current
Hybrid document, relationship, cycle, verdict, and reconciliation tables into a bounded reporter
projection. Accept old schema-v1 reports while schema-v2 reports atomically replace one instance's
bounded inventory and append only real artifact transitions. Render per-instance Work and History
surfaces with stable IDs, sanitized titles, lifecycle distinctions, relationship context,
freshness, explicit partial-state and divergence warnings, and semantic SSE refresh.

## Contract Decisions

- Project Maps are first-class; the visible chain is Idea → Map → PRM → Campaign.
- Stable UUIDs and visible IDs are canonical; titles are sanitized and capped at 160 characters.
- Document lifecycle, outcome lifecycle, outcome disposition, and reconciliation are separate.
- Snapshot ownership is per instance. Divergent instances are displayed, never silently merged.
- Inventory is capped at 500 artifacts with `total_count` and `truncated`; a partial snapshot is
  labelled and does not claim complete project truth.
- Transition payloads are capped at 50 events and hosted retention remains 90 days.
- The first schema-v2 snapshot creates inventory but no invented transition history.
- Unchanged reports and heartbeats do not append lifecycle history or trigger semantic refresh.
- Existing generic material events remain supported as a separate operational supplement.

## Work2 Boundary

Implement, run the quickest meaningful changed-path validation, commit the scoped candidate,
deploy it to the configured combined `ts.rookaro.com` work target, check public health plus
authenticated/API behavior with safe fixtures or the deployed service, register the candidate and
its open owning chain in the release cohort, checkpoint and rebuild-prove Hybrid state, and run
strict Doctor.

Do not push, tag, publish a Tool Shed release, synchronize disconnected clients, or mark the
Campaign, PRM, Map, or Idea terminal at Work2.

